  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "psf-md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## PSF sweep: look at the frames\n",
    "\n",
    "For one frame, measured / blurred model / difference at each PSF sigma. The forward model has no\n",
    "detector blur (`psf_sigma=0.0`), so if the detector is blurring intensity, the right sigma should\n",
    "visibly flatten the difference panel.\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses the package's own `psf_taps`, which builds the DISCRETE Gaussian `exp(-s^2) I_|t|(s^2)` --\n",
    "a sampled Gaussian aliases below ~0.7 px (sigma 0.3 realises as 0.09), so `gaussian_filter` is the\n",
    "wrong tool for exactly this test."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "psf-sweep",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1500x2820 with 36 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from holotomocupy.psf import psf_taps, psf_blur\n",
    "\n",
    "PSF_FRAME  = 171                                      # which frame to look at\n",
    "PSF_SIGMAS = [0.0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 1.0, 1.5]\n",
    "\n",
    "meas, mod, _ = store[PSF_FRAME]\n",
    "mg, dg = cp.asarray(meas), cp.asarray(mod)\n",
    "\n",
    "nrow = len(PSF_SIGMAS)\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(nrow, 3, figsize=(15, 4.7 * nrow))\n",
    "lo, hi = np.percentile(meas[c_], [1, 99])\n",
    "for i, s in enumerate(PSF_SIGMAS):\n",
    "    w = psf_taps(s)[1]\n",
    "    m2 = dg if w is None else psf_blur(dg, w)\n",
    "    dif = cp.asnumpy(mg - m2)\n",
    "    m2n = cp.asnumpy(m2)\n",
    "    v = np.percentile(np.abs(dif[c_]), 99)\n",
    "    for j, (img, t, kw) in enumerate((\n",
    "            (meas, f'measured (frame {PSF_FRAME})', dict(cmap='gray', vmin=lo, vmax=hi)),\n",
    "            (m2n,  f'model, PSF sigma {s:.1f} px', dict(cmap='gray', vmin=lo, vmax=hi)),\n",
    "            (dif,  'measured - model', dict(cmap='seismic', vmin=-v, vmax=v)))):\n",
    "        a = ax[i, j]\n",
    "        im = a.imshow(img, **kw)\n",
    "        a.set_title(t, fontsize=10)\n",
    "        a.set_xticks([]); a.set_yticks([])\n",
    "        fig.colorbar(im, ax=a, fraction=0.046)\n",
    "del mg, dg\n",
    "cp.get_default_memory_pool().free_all_blocks()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
